prefix: `[yalla][security]`\n    14\t- Optional: encrypt with the maintainer's p
ublic key (linked from\n    15\t  <https://github.com/JuribaDev>)\n    16\t\n   
17\tWhat to include:\n    18\t\n    19\t1. The yalla version (`yalla version --j
son`).\n    20\t2. Reproduction steps, including the exact command line and any\
n    21\t   redacted log excerpts.\n    22\t3. The impact you observed (token le
ak, RCE, denial-of-service,\n    23\t   privilege escalation, etc.).\n    24\t\n
   25\tYou will receive an acknowledgement within **3 business days**. We aim\n 
  26\tto ship a fix or mitigation within **30 days** for high-severity\n    27\t
issues; lower-severity issues are folded into the next scheduled\n    28\treleas
e.\n    29\t\n    30\t## Supported Versions\n    31\t\n    32\tPre-1.0 yalla sup
ports only the latest minor release line on\n    33\t[GitHub Releases](https://g
ithub.com/JuribaDev/yalla/releases). Once\n    34\tyalla reaches 1.0 the matrix 
will be published here.\n    35\t\n    36\t## Threat Model and Hard Rules\n    3
7\t\n    38\tYalla is invoked by AI agents in unattended pipelines. The followin
g\n    39\tproperties are part of the public contract and are enforced by the\n 
  40\ttest suite:\n    41\t\n    42\t- **Secrets never reach stdout.** `--json` 
data on stdout, all\n    43\t  diagnostics on stderr. The `--token` value, well-
known transport\n    44\t  patterns (`Authorization`, `X-Api-Key`, `X-Auth-Token
`), and\n    45\t  `?token=`/`?api_key=` query strings are scrubbed by\n    46\t
 `internal/output.Redactor` before any byte is written.\n    47\t- **Errors are 
typed.** Every user-visible failure is an\n    48\t  `internal/errors.Error` wit
h a stable `Code` and exit code. Plain\n    49\t  `fmt.Errorf` reaching stderr i
s a contract violation.\n    50\t- **`--no-input` never hangs.** When the flag i
s set, any prompt path\n    51\t  exits with `E_NO_INPUT_REQUIRED` (exit code 9)
instead of blocking.\n    52\t- **Releases are reproducible.** Archives are buil
t by GoReleaser in\n    53\t  GitHub Actions; checksums are published alongside 
every release.\n    54\t  The npm wrapper, Homebrew formula, Scoop manifest, and
WinGet\n    55\t  manifest all resolve to the same archives.\n    56\t\n    57\t
